# Learn Go Pointers

Understand how pointers work, when to use them, and how to avoid common mistakes.

## Sections

1. **basics** - Declaring, dereferencing, and passing pointers
2. **structs** - Linked list built with `*Node`
3. **receivers** - Value receiver vs pointer receiver comparison
4. **memory** - `unsafe.Sizeof`, `new` vs `make`

## How to Run

` + "```" + `bash
go run main.go
go test ./...
` + "```" + `

## Key Rules

| Concept | Guideline |
|---------|-----------|
| `&x` | Take address of variable `x` |
| `*p` | Dereference pointer `p` to get/set the value |
| Value receiver | Does NOT modify original; use for small, immutable structs |
| Pointer receiver | DOES modify original; use when mutation or large struct |
| nil check | Always guard against nil before dereferencing |
| `new(T)` | Allocate zeroed `T`, return `*T` |
| `make(T, ...)` | Initialize slices, maps, channels (not arbitrary types) |
